    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0752" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">War Trade Board Files: Japanese Tonnage
                    Negotiations, Vol. II</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the British Ministry of
                        Shipping</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fisher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chairman of the War Trade Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCormick</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">S 173</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 31, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. McCormick</hi>: In accordance with your suggestion,. I have
                    already consulted Mr. Gay in this
                        matter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d601-f1"/> and I am happy to say that as a
                    result of urgent representations, the Ministry of Shipping in London have agreed
                    to take no action pending further consultation in order that we may jointly
                    decide what is best to be-done in the common interest.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Fisher</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d601-f1" n="1" xml:id="d601-f1-content">
                <p>The chartering of Japanese vessels.</p>
            </note>
